        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "\n\nNow I can see the issue. In `/workspace/pkg/clustermesh/common/remote_cluster.go:272-309`, the `getClusterConfig` function creates a channel `cfgch` and uses a controller to send the configuration through it. The problem is:\n\n1. Line 272: `cfgch := make(chan types.CiliumClusterConfig)` - unbuffered channel\n2. Line 290: `cfgch <- config` - blocking send\n3. Line 299-307: The select waits for either the config or context cancellation\n\nWhen the context is cancelled (line 259), the select at line 299 returns via `<-ctx.Done()`, but the controller may still execute line 290 and try to send on the unbuffered channel, causing a deadlock.\n\nLet me search for tests to understand the expected behavior better:\n\n",
