          "type": "text",
          "text": "\n\nNow I understand the issue completely. The problem is in the `getClusterConfig` function at line 272 in `/workspace/pkg/clustermesh/common/remote_cluster.go`. When an unbuffered channel is used and the context gets cancelled, the receiver exits but the controller may still try to send on the channel, causing a deadlock.\n\nThe fix is to use a **buffered channel** with capacity 1, so the send operation never blocks even if the receiver has already exited:\n\n",
