        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "\n\nExcellent! The tests compile successfully. Let me provide a summary of the fix:\n\n## Summary\n\nThe deadlock issue in the clustermesh subsystem has been fixed by changing the channel used for configuration retrieval from unbuffered to buffered.\n\n**Root Cause:** In `/workspace/pkg/clustermesh/common/remote_cluster.go:270`, the `getClusterConfig` function used an unbuffered channel (`cfgch := make(chan types.CiliumClusterConfig)`) to communicate the fetched configuration from a background controller to the main goroutine. When the context was cancelled during shutdown:\n\n1. The select statement at line 299 would return via `<-ctx.Done()`\n2. The main goroutine would exit the function\n3. The background controller might still attempt to send the configuration via `cfgch <- config` (line 291)\n4. Since the channel was unbuffered and the receiver had already exited, the send would block indefinitely\n5. This caused a deadlock preventing the controller from terminating\n\n**Fix:** Changed line 270 from:\n```go\ncfgch := make(chan types.CiliumClusterConfig)\n```\nto:\n```go\ncfgch := make(chan types.CiliumClusterConfig, 1)\n```\n\nBy using a buffered channel with capacity 1, the send operation will never block even if the receiver has already exited. The buffered slot guarantees that the controller can always complete its send, allowing proper shutdown and eliminating the deadlock scenario.",
          "time": {
            "start": 1782151530022,
            "end": 1782151530078
          },
          "id": "prt_ef0824626001CaV2IOf88k7l3g",
          "sessionID": "ses_10f87afe8ffeQMzPi0vQdFIF71",
          "messageID": "msg_ef08201d00014xLj1N46gzlFli"
        },
